WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.320
Do you have a license?!

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.820
You better

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:06.300
Government often demands you get a license

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.620
before you're allowed to work.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:10.759
People think this is a good idea.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.100
We license drivers,

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:13.800
we license dogs,

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.000
People think it makes us safer.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.220
But licenses also do something bad.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:21.840
If people want to work, let them work.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.160
11-year old Madison Root was told

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:25.340
she couldn’t work

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.340
because she didn’t have a license.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.100
She wanted money for braces, so

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.420
she tried selling mistletoe.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.940
Here she is in a tree, picking it.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:36.840
But when she went to sell it at this outdoor market

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.580
police told her “Stop!

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.880
That’s illegal!”

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.980
They told her she could beg,

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:43.860
but can't sell anything.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.800
Her father sent us this video.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:49.340
I was amazed that people cannot

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.660
work hard,

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:54.000
but they can be just lazy.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.360
I assume that’s not exactly what the cops

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:58.060
but the fact is:

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:01.020
All over America, people want to work, but can't

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.960
because it’s so hard to get proper licenses.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.440
In the 1950s, well

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.440
only about 1 in 20 Americans

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.140
needed the government’s blessing to do their job

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:13.000
Today that number is more than 1 in 3.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.300
This new book, Bottleneckers,

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.640
reveals how licensing rules allow

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:18.740
older businesses to profit

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:20.700
by keeping newcomers out.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.780
These are people who want to erect barriers,

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:24.780
who want to put in place bottlenecks because

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.580
they want to keep competitors out.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.220
It's kind of like what happens on a highway

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:30.840
if you close a lane.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:33.580
The established, existing businesses are like

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:34.900
these motorcycles

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:37.080
licenses don’t slow them down.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:38.780
During my consumer report days,

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:43.400
I assumed licenses protected us from scams like these:

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.430
We are not ripping people off.

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:48.320
But licensing doesn’t stop that.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.820
Georgia funeral director,

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:52.940
who was pitching dead bodies out in the woods

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:55.080
behind his funeral establishment.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:56.290
He was licensed.

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:57.560
Bernie Madoff

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:58.990
was licensed.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:01.680
Teachers in public schools who have sex with their students.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:02.600
Licensed.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.640
Licensing doesn’t stop that.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.260
What licensing does do,

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:08.200
is crush new entrepreneurs.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:10.820
Want to braid peoples hair?

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:13.120
This woman was told she couldn’t do it legally

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:15.260
unless she spent thousands of hours

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:18.080
to get a cosmetology license.

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:19.520
She begged the government,

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:20.960
"Just let me braid!"

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:22.140
I was making these phone calls

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:23.680
to the board of cosmetology

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:25.920
saying I don't want to do

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:26.880
cosmetology

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:29.319
All I want to do is braid hair.

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:30.080
No!

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.080
Not without our license,

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.820
said the cosmetology board.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:34.820
These are people

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.920
who have a clear conflict of interest.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:37.940
Of course they do,

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:39.700
She wants to compete with them

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:41.500
Cosmetologists got together

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:43.800
and they went to the legislature and they lobbied

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.340
for the creation of a license.

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:47.260
Makes me wonder,

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.440
how could I get rid of my competition?

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.730
I’m annoyed by all these TV channels.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:53.800
I’d like to limit that.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.380
Yes, I’m sure.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:56.960
So what you need to do John

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:58.700
is you need to go to government

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:00.920
and ask for special protection.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:03.580
You need to claim that there is some public interest,

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:05.220
some way that the public

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:06.780
is going to be protected

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:09.300
by limiting the number of providers.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:11.380
And that actually happened in&nbsp;America.

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:12.820
When I started in TV,

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:14.220
most viewers just had

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:19.000
ABC, CBS, NBC, and boring public television.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.620
People could have had many more channels,

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:24.340
cable TV technology was available.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:26.880
But lobbyists for my employer argued:

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:28.800
“No! That will hurt the poor.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:31.200
They need broadcast TV.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.840
They can’t afford cable.

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:36.460
So the FCC limited cable TV for years.

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:38.379
And that helped me make more money.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:41.140
Certainly it does, that’s the effect of licensing.

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:41.740
That is,

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:43.820
the people who are in the industry have the ability

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:46.160
to artificially inflate prices

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.360
and their wages as a result

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.900
and consumers are worse off.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:49.840
I was better off!

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:51.140
You were much better off

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:52.560
but now we realize

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:53.940
everyone else was worse off.

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:55.930
That’s what the bottle neck does

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:57.380
It limits choices,

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.060
thereby raising prices,

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:01.320
and enriching older businesses

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.110
There are so many bottlenecks.

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:05.180
We’ll show you a bunch in the next episodes.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:06.840
We’ll also show you how these

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:08.840
problems can be better solved

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:10.020
by the free market.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:12.180
Market regulation actually is enough for the

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.860
vast majority of occupations out there.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:16.800
Bottleneckers around America,

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:18.800
They make life worse for you.

